L001394	Following conventions in the literature, we could call the states $P_k|\psi\rangle$ (up to normalization)  ``superselection sectors".  Proposition \ref{prop:superselection}, whose simple proof is omitted for brevity, tells us that $(R,\delta)$-SSB is sufficient to ensure that the symmetric state $|\psi\rangle$ is well-approximated by any of the superselection sectors $P_k|\psi\rangle$ to physical observables that are sufficiently local.
