L001427	The two simple propositions above ensure that a state $|\psi\rangle$, formally defined in Definition \ref{def:quantumSSB}, satisfies all the criteria that a physicist would expect for a many-body state with SSB.  With a meaningful criterion for how to discuss SSB in  quantum states that involve a macroscopically large (but nevertheless finite) number of degrees of freedom, we may now go on to show that the QPC implies SSB: if the quantum ground state of $H_0$ has SSB, then $H_0+V$ will also have SSB as long as $V$ is locally symmetric and sufficiently small.
